<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalhora dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1701–<a href="/years/1783">1783</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Kalhoras</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kalhora dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> from about 1701 to 1783, first as governors under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and later as tributaries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani</a> rulers. Of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> origins, the Kalhoras built canals and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a> as their capital in 1768. After they killed Talpur leaders, the Talpurs overthrew them at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-halani">Battle of Halani</a> in 1783.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalhora-dynasty.jpg" alt="Kalhora dynasty" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PavelD · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
